.nh
.TH "PB-API-TOKEN-REVOKE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-api-token-revoke - Revoke an API token


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb api-token revoke <name|id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Revoke an API token by name or id. Requests that use it fail from then on.
You can revoke your own tokens; owners and admins can revoke any member's.
A name shared by several members' tokens must be given as an id. Without
--yes, the command asks for confirmation first.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for revoke

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	revoke without asking


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb api-token revoke deploy
  pb api-token revoke apitok_123 --yes
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-api-token(1)\fP
